  {
   "gap": "No second host, no EKS/S3 in this container: the replays ran on the same container and CPU class as the producer (L0, 4 shared cores). Counted cost does not depend on the host, so the replays are valid; the wall-time columns (ns/GAE, end-to-end wall) are not independently reproduced.",
   "id": "G1-no-second-host"
  },
  {
   "gap": "Every replay used target/release/ecbench (sha256 b4fcf0ecdb3d0a0f42842856fe1e258258d52414c3ea54155292ae5431a592a0), the binary that produced the sessions. No cargo build was allowed, so there is no from-source rebuild as in research/ic_tableb_binary_ksum_20261115/validator. The independent checks are (a) a re-execution of all 480 deterministic runs per session by a different session than the producer's, (b) the validator's own Python prime-field arithmetic ([recovered]G == target for every record), and (c) an own recompute of every headline from records.jsonl.",
   "id": "G2-same-binary"
  },
  {
   "gap": "No pcc claim filed and no keyring signature on the certificate or the report: every statement here is [pcc:unverified]. AGENTS.md 'Sabotage is assumed' asks for signed artifacts; none could be produced in this container.",
   "id": "G3-no-pcc-or-keyring"
  },
  {
   "gap": "bitop/v1 ratios are recomputed from each record's own work.bitops_per_sqrt_r field; the per-primitive bitop widths behind that field were not re-derived (the unit's definition is the producer's).",
   "id": "G4-bitop-not-rederived"
  },
  {
   "gap": "L0 runs, no isolation tier and no native L2/replay/A/A admission: valid for counted cost only; no wall-time or L2 claim is validated.",
   "id": "G5-no-isolation"
